# Terraform's working files. Never commit them: a local init leaves hundreds
# of megabytes of providers in .terraform/, and a state file or a saved plan
# maps the whole account (a binary plan is not redacted the way a rendered one
# is). The lock file (.terraform.lock.hcl) IS committed: both inits run with
# -lockfile=readonly.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info
*.tfplan
tfplan
plan.txt
# scripts/host-apply.sh's saved plans and their renderings (host.yml).
tfplan-*
plan-*.txt
crash.log
crash.*.log
.terraformrc
terraform.rc
# Local overrides would change what is applied without showing in review.
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
# Variable files may hold personal values (an address, a zone id); keep them
# local. production.tfvars is the exception: it holds only non-personal
# settings and infra.yml reads it, so it is committed.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!production.tfvars
# Never commit an env file of secret values.
*.env
